Fixes a crash in WriteThread::EnterAsBatchGroupLeader on aarch64 builds
without LSE atomics: a spurious compare_exchange_weak failure while
re-linking the writers that could not join the write group walked past the
end of the writer queue. compare_exchange_strong cannot fail spuriously.
From Stalwart's RocksDB branch (stalwartlabs/rocksdb, stalwart/11.8.1, the
one commit it adds to v11.8.1; submitted upstream as facebook/rocksdb#15415,
not in 11.13.2). Stalwart's bundled RocksDB carries it; this system RocksDB,
which Stalwart links instead, carries it too.

--- a/db/write_thread.cc	2026-11-12 19:22:32.784807466 -0500
+++ b/db/write_thread.cc	2026-11-12 19:22:32.792807330 -0500
@@ -559,7 +559,8 @@
     rb->link_older = we;
     re->link_newer = nullptr;
     we->link_newer = rb;
-    if (!newest_writer_.compare_exchange_weak(w, re)) {
+    // Strong: the walk below assumes a failure means newer writers arrived.
+    if (!newest_writer_.compare_exchange_strong(w, re)) {
       while (w->link_older != newest_writer) {
         w = w->link_older;
       }
